    description: "Every spell symbol exists within this tome — contents determined by Pandro and how much access he permits. The Grimoire cannot be read by anyone but Pandro. Sealed state: Mono (the fifteen elemental spirit forms) recommends spells from the active elemental domain. The more powerful the spell, the more of Irane's mana Pandro draws on. That power is addicting. The more he draws, the more he wants. He IS the constraint within himself — the only point of restraint in an infinite spell archive. His battle is not with enemies. It is with the Grimoire itself.\n\n**Kazemi's Nexus — the Will-Activation Merged State.** During the Will-activation cascade at Urial's birth (§lore 9.6c), the sealed-state restriction (one Grannie, one elemental domain at a time) is overridden entirely. Pandro does not simply gain access to more spells — the Grimoire's infinite combinatorial library becomes an active, self-directing process rather than a reference he consults, and Pandro experiences it as walking through the library itself, which is, in this state, his own core. He starts anchored to a single element and accumulates more as the state runs, each new element compounding onto what he already holds, until he is functionally a living spell: the start and the end of a working that continues altering itself until its objective is fulfilled. Fifteen marks appear across his body — two per limb, three across his back — one per element, tracking which domains are currently open to him.",
