    description: "Not worn over the skin but fused with it — a living, additional layer that taps directly into the cores of Irane's own dead skin cells the way scales tap into a dragon's hide. Formally, among the three Empiric-class weapons, this is **the Empiric Armour** — Sanctuary informally. Its defining trait is that it 'naturally and instinctively' alters its own composition to counter whatever mana last struck it, a permanent, always-on version of the reactive-body mechanic Domination was originally built to override — Sanctuary does not need Domination's authorship to redirect it; it reacts continuously, on its own. First deployed in full at 75–80% output during the climactic Empiric-class battle against Vraka and Selis, alongside its paired spear, S-Apexia (the Empiric Spear), and later joined by Deliverance (the Empiric Bow).\n\nOnce Irane sits the throne, Sanctuary becomes literally the power core of Paradise: every major and minor mana requirement in the capital — shielding, transport, the city's own living architecture — runs directly off Irane's core output through the armor. 'The armor guards the city' is not a figure of speech inside Apexia; it is the electrical and mana grid. Requires the wielder's Drive/Will state above 50% to function at all.",
    corrosion: 'Direct contact from anyone but Irane is dangerous by design — Isoke is warned off touching it at close range during the coronation, told plainly she would be consumed and destroyed for trying while his core is still running at sustained high output.',
