    description: "The Empiric-class spear — **the Empiric Spear** — drawn directly from the core of Kazemi and the many core-cells beneath it — including, once claimed, every Valariyan core Irane has been given. Formally 'S-Apexia' when drawn in full; 'Apexia' informally. Its signature and most disturbing mechanic: every strike is marked with Irane's own Death-Will core, such that no blow from it is ever literally fatal — but the sensation and full memory of death is inflicted on the target's own core in full, repeatedly, permanently legible to that core afterward, without the mercy of the death actually ending. This is mechanically why Vraka and Selis survive the final battle at all — their own binding contract (§lore 9.7h) required a literal winner and a signature, and a dead opponent cannot sign a contract — and why they end the battle not merely defeated but genuinely, permanently afraid of him, having each experienced total death, over and over, with no release.\n\nCan reshape mid-flight into elemental spear-forms drawing on any of the fifteen Pillars, target multiple opponents with independent trajectories simultaneously, and command the mana of any core below its own wielder's level within its effective range.",
