    seat: null,
    designation: 'Ascended Art — Bifurcation Mechanic · Practitioner: Kazemi (conceptual)',
    description: "Not a weapon in the ordinary sense — an Art, the mechanism by which the conceptual Kazemi builds and installs a genuinely separate human identity into the world: Irane C. Kazemi, the man who fights, feels, and forgets alongside everyone else, distinct from the 88-million-year conceptual mind that made him. The Art works from a bank of up to one hundred pre-built human bodies, each engineered to the same standard as the Valariyan Ascended-tier forms, reserved for exactly this purpose rather than issued to ordinary converts.\n\n**The mechanic.** Kazemi's own cell-cycle — die, adapt, reforge, improve — scaled up to the level of an entire identity. Rather than housing his full conceptual self in a single body permanently, Kazemi steps back into a dormant, dream-like state above roughly fifty percent output, while a human perspective — sharing his core, his memories only up to the point of the trial's end, and none of the trial itself — takes the seat below it. The two are not separate beings competing for the same throne; they are the same core viewed from two different bands of the same percentage scale, the human half genuinely unaware, most of the time, of what sits above him. When the human body is used up, or when the moment calls for it, the Art rebuilds a fresh vessel from the reserve and reseats the same continuous identity into it — a resurrection that looks, from outside, like the Emperor simply appearing again the next morning.\n\n**The payoff — Lord Kazemi and Lord Irane.** The Art's clearest on-page use gives the two halves their working titles directly, in a face-to-face conversation between them: a Primordial encased in a core is what a conceptual actually is, and Irane is confirmed, by his own count, to have killed no one in his first true act as a fully independent human self — the clean, quiet answer at the center of the entire trial's moral question. Lord Kazemi is the conceptual, the god the Valariyan's kneel to; Lord Irane is the man, fallible and still learning to be one, who leads them day to day. Kazemi's Rebirth is what keeps that division from collapsing back into a single, unbounded being.",
