    currentHolder: 'irane',
    notes: "Part 9.3.2/9.5. The mechanism behind the human/conceptual split first announced in Part 8 and given its full payoff scene in 9.5 — the direct Kazemi/Irane conversation that confirms the titles 'Lord Kazemi' and 'Lord Irane.' Per the post-bifurcation power correction: human Lord Irane does not casually wield trial-era cosmic techniques (no Universal Implosion, no fifteen-dragon split, no Dragon's Roar, no perfect technique-recall) — he fights and governs as a strong, still-fallible man with one reduced-scale Enari and his forged weapons, genuinely below Arai/Hope/Zoe's own peak. The conceptual Lord Kazemi half can only resurface if Irane's body is at genuine risk of dying and he consents to it live, in the moment — never as a casual power escalation. See id: hot-hands-of-time, id: noxas-book, §lore 9.7c–9.7d.",
