    description: "A ceremonial blade forged for the Spirits by Elorah and Selis a thousand years before the Theomachy, named for its first wielder, Masamune Honjo, remembered as the God of the Blade — a mythical figure said to command every element from Fire to Darkness through a rare Harmonic-Light core. Passed down only to a Spirit judged the era's finest swordsman, the blade carries a genuine, accumulating kill-history: roughly seventeen million lives taken across its thousand-year existence, with a stated, terrible threshold of one trillion lives before it fully \"awakens.\"\n\n**The absorption.** Forge Neel — the blade's last free wielder, and one of the most feared warriors in Spirit territory — fought Dokia Caedus to a standstill during the extraction assault on Hope's stronghold, landing what should have been a killing thrust through her heart. Dokia's own nature made the exchange survivable for her and fatal for him in a different sense: her Life/Death Art forced Forge to experience, in a single locked instant, the deaths inflicted by every prior wielder of Masamune, including the original Masamune Honjo's own declaration that the blade would take a trillion lives before waking — and Forge, breaking under the weight of that shared history, surrendered. Dokia then took the blade for herself, using her Will just long enough to absorb Masamune's full kill-history and desire directly into her own core, before reforging the exchange in reverse: Forge's own soul was fused into the blade, and the blade's awakened, hungry will was fused into a new Human-Tool body built from Forge's captured form.\n\nThe result is a single being serving two functions at once: Masamune, the sentient weapon-consciousness — the accumulated wills of every past master, all sharing the desire to kill and reach the trillion-life threshold — now speaks and acts with full autonomy in a human-shaped Tool body, while Forge Neel's own consciousness is trapped inside the physical blade itself, forced to experience every kill Masamune commits as his own, unable to stop it, unable to die from it. Masamune bows to Dokia as \"Kazemi's Death\" and serves her without hesitation; Forge screams from inside the blade with every kill tallied toward the goal he never chose.",
